Linear discriminant analysis (LDA) is a widely-used feature extraction method in classiﬁcation.&#13;
However, the original LDA has limitations due to assumption of unimodal structure for each cluster, which not satisﬁed many applications such as facial image data when variations, e.g. angle and illumination, can signiﬁcantly inﬂuence images. In this paper, we propose novel called hierarchical (h-LDA), takes into account subcluster structures the&#13;
data formulation algorithm. We develop theoretical basis by identifying its relation two-way multivariate variance (MANOVA) based on model decomposition. Furthermore, an efﬁcient algorithm regularized version h-LDA (h-RLDA) presented using QR decomposition generalized SVD. To validate&#13;
the effectiveness proposed method, compare face recognition performance among h-RLDA, LDA, PCA, TensorFaces. Our experiments show that h-RLDA produces better prediction accuracy than other methods. When only small subset features are used (reduced dimensionality), superiority over methods becomes more signiﬁcant. It also shown computationally much alternative
